{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"# LLM-Review -1 on 1639 was `bugfix-size-attestation` — attestation now EARNED (plan review PASS, signed)\n\nChange 1639 got **Verified +1** (CI green) but **LLM-Review -1**, with one blocking finding:\n`bugfix-size-attestation` — 483 non-test lines against the 150-line floor for a bug, and this\nticket held no plan-review attestation. Per policy the remedy is to EARN the attestation, not to\nshrink the diff, so I ran `rebar review-plan`.\n\n**It blocked four times before passing, and every block was a genuine gap in the plan rather than\ngate noise.** The code was never the problem — in each case the plan text failed to state a\ndecision the implementation had already made. Fixed in order:\n\n1. **P4 oversize (deterministic)** — the description was 8333 chars against the 8000 admission\n   limit. Trimmed to 7999; the measured evidence it shed is preserved in the comments above and on\n   2a76, so nothing was lost.\n2. **AC1 raced the detached child (E6/E2)** — AC1 said the test asserts the marker exists \"after\n   the detached child exits\", but the child is `start_new_session=True` and deliberately NEVER\n   waited, so nothing said HOW the test synchronizes. The test already polls the marker path on a\n   bounded 60s/0.1s deadline; AC1 now states that poll IS the synchronization contract for this\n   limb, so the assertion is deterministic rather than racy.\n3. **D5 undercounted the write tools (E4/G1G2)** — the plan said \"the ten `-> str` tools\"; there\n   are **eleven**. Verified against the pre-change file: 11 match `) -> str:`. The eleventh,\n   `declare_no_file_impact`, is `structured_output=False` and pinned in `NO_SCHEMA_EXEMPT` by\n   `test_no_schema_exempt_set_is_accurate`, so it advertises no outputSchema to extend and\n   migrating it would regress that guard. The implementation already excluded it; the plan now\n   says so and names it as the one documented gap.\n4. **D4 was silent on the commit-phase reasons (G6)** — the choke point also carries\n   `stage-failed` / `commit-failed` / `commit-lock-timeout` and the recovery reasons, which D4's\n   four-item non-recorded list did not mention. Those ARE recorded, deliberately: a write that\n   never got COMMITTED also never reached the remote and is invisible on the same surfaces, so\n   `pending` plus a `reason` naming the phase beats silence. That decision was already in\n   `record_failure`'s docstring; it is now in the plan too.\n5. **Limb 4 had no AC (E6/E1/COH)** — the reconciler was diagnosed but unverified. Added **AC7**:\n   it is fixed STRUCTURALLY, not by a fourth code path, because `push_state` records to disk\n   regardless of which logger root holds a handler — the sole reason limb 4 was mute — and that is\n   pinned by the AC3 drive asserting recording works with NO handler on the `rebar` root.\n\n**Result: `review-plan` verdict PASS, attestation signed at head_sha `e78dadb4be`** — the same\ncommit as patchset 1, so the attestation is current for the change under review.\n\n`rerun-llm-review` posted on 1639 with that rebuttal. No code changed, so CI stays green; awaiting\nthe re-vote."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786521296868226001,"uuid":"2baadecc-f682-4d38-8952-47653332a510"}